          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The Poisson sigma model was first considered in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noriaki+Ikeda"}> Noriaki Ikeda
              ,
              %em Two-dimensional gravity and nonlinear gauge theory
              , Ann.Phys.
              %strong 235
              (1994) 435- 464 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9312059"}> hep-th/9312059
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aphy.1994.1104"} doi:10.1006/aphy.1994.1104
          %p
            and later independently by P. Schaller, T. Strobl, motivated from an attempt to unify several two-dimensional models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            and to cast them into a common form with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                P. Schaller, T. Strobl,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Poisson structure induced (topological) field theories
                %strong 9
                (1994), no. 33, 3129–3136 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1142/S0217732394002951"}> doi:10.1142/S0217732394002951
                \&amp;rbrack;;
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Introduction to Poisson
                    = succeed "-models" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 469
            %li
              %p
                Thomas Strobl,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravity from Lie algebroid morphisms
                %strong 246
                (2004), no. 3, 475–502,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebroid Yang-Mills theories
                %strong 93
                (2004), no. 21, 211601, 4 pp. &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.93.211601"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.93.211601
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Bojowald"}> Martin Bojowald
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Kotov"} Alexei Kotov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie algebroid morphisms, Poisson sigma models, and off-shell closed gauge symmetries
                = succeed ":4" do
                  %strong 54
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2004.11.002"} doi:10.1016/j.geomphys.2004.11.002
            %li
              %p
                Ctirad Klimčík, T. Strobl,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em WZW-Poisson manifolds
                %strong 43
                (2002), no. 4, 341–344 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/S0393-0440(02)00027-X"}> doi:10.1016/S0393-0440(02)00027-X
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The detailed argument by Cattaneo and Felder on how
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"} Maxim Kontsevich
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            star product is the 3-point function of the Poisson sigma-model is in
          %ul
            %li#CattaneoFelder2000
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A path integral approach to the Kontsevich quantization formula
                %strong 212
                (2000) 591–611 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s002200000229"}> doi:10.1007/s002200000229
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9902090"} math.QA/9902090
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Poisson sigma models and deformation quantization
                %strong 16
                (2001) 179–190 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0102208"}> hep-th/0102208
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217732301003255"} doi:10.1142/S0217732301003255
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                %em Poisson sigma models and symplectic groupoids
                , (ed.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              %p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003023"}> math.SG/0003023
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the AKSZ formulation of the Poisson sigma model
                %strong 56
                (2001) 163–179 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0102108"}> math.QA/0102108
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1010963926853"} doi:10.1023/A:1010963926853
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              Nima Moshayedi:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kontsevich’s Deformation Quantization and Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-05122-7"} doi:10.1007/978-3-031-05122-7
          %p
            Interpretation in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/infinity-Chern-Simons+theory"} infinity-Chern-Simons theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/AKSZ+Sigma-Models+in+Higher+Chern-Weil+Theory"} AKSZ Sigma-Models in Higher Chern-Weil Theory
              (2011)
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holography
          %ul
            %li#Vassilevich
              D. V. Vassilevich,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holographic duals to Poisson sigma models
              %strong 87
              (2013) 104011 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.7029"}> arXiv:1301.7029
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.87.104011"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.87.104011
          %h3#LitWithBranes With branes
          %p
            The study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            in the Poisson sigma-model has been started in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Damien+Calaque"}> Damien Calaque
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bimodules and branes in deformation quantization
                %strong 147
                (2011) 105-160 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.2299"}> arXiv:0908.2299
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/S0010437X10004847"} doi:10.1112/S0010437X10004847
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Damien+Calaque"}> Damien Calaque
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation quantization with generators and relations
                %strong 337
                (2011) 1-12 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.4377"}> arXiv:0911.4377
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2011.03.037"} doi:10.1016/j.jalgebra.2011.03.037
            %li#CattaneoFelder03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Coisotropic submanifolds in Poisson geometry and branes in the Poisson
                    = succeed "-model" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %strong 69
                (2004) 157-175 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309180"}> arXiv:0309180
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11005-004-0609-7"} doi:10.1007/s11005-004-0609-7
            %li
              %p
                Andrea Ferrario,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Poisson Sigma Model with branes and hyperelliptic Riemann surfaces
                %strong 49
                (2008) 092301 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.0635"}> arXiv:0709.0635
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.2982234"} doi:10.1063/1.2982234
          %p A review is in
          %ul
            %li
              F. Falceto,
              %em Branes in Poisson sigma models
              (2009) (
              %a{:href => "http://benasque.org/2009gph/talks_contr/094Falceto.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#further_developments Further developments
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Francesco Bonechi,
                = succeed "," do
